# NOIR ROAST — environment variables. This file contains NAMES AND EXPLANATIONS ONLY.
# Never put a real value in it, and never commit a real .env file (.env and .env.* are git-ignored).
#
# There are four different places a value can live. Using the wrong one is how secrets leak:
#
#   1. Browser build (Vite)         VITE_* variables.  Everything here is PUBLIC: it ships inside the
#                                    JavaScript bundle. Local dev: .env.local.  Vercel: Project Settings >
#                                    Environment Variables (Production / Preview / Development).
#   2. Supabase Edge Function       Set with `supabase secrets set NAME=value` (hosted) or from your shell
#      secrets                       when running the local stack. NEVER in Vercel, NEVER in the repo.
#   3. Platform-injected            SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY are provided to
#                                    Edge Functions automatically. Do not set them yourself.
#   4. Your own shell / CI          Only for tooling (e.g. SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN for the CLI). Never committed.

# =====================================================================================================
# 1) BROWSER (public) — copy these into .env.local for local development, and into Vercel for deploys
# =====================================================================================================

# Supabase project URL, e.g. https://<project-ref>.supabase.co  (local stack: http://127.0.0.1:54321)
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=

# Supabase "anon" / publishable key. Public by design: Row Level Security is what protects the data.
# NEVER use the service-role / secret key here.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Razorpay KEY ID only (rzp_test_... in test mode, rzp_live_... in live mode). Optional: used just to show a
# "test mode" banner on the checkout page before an order exists. The checkout session itself carries the key id
# from the server. NEVER put the Razorpay key SECRET here.
VITE_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=

# Optional: public site origin used for canonical URLs and auth redirect links, e.g. https://www.example.com
# Defaults to the current origin.
VITE_SITE_URL=

# =====================================================================================================
# 2) EDGE FUNCTION SECRETS (server only) — `supabase secrets set NAME=value`
# =====================================================================================================
# RAZORPAY_KEY_ID           same key id as above (rzp_test_... first). Used to create orders on the server.
# RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET       Razorpay key secret. Server only. Signs/verifies payments.
# RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET   The secret you type when creating the webhook in the Razorpay dashboard.
#                           Webhook URL: https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/functions/v1/razorpay-webhook
#                           Events: payment.authorized, payment.captured, payment.failed, order.paid, refund.processed
# ALLOWED_ORIGIN            (optional) lock CORS to your site, e.g. https://www.example.com  (default: *)
# RAZORPAY_API_BASE         (optional, tests only) point at a fake Razorpay server. Leave unset in real environments.
#
# Safety net built into the code: a payment key starting rzp_live_ is REFUSED while any price or weight is still
# marked provisional, or while shipping/tax are not marked confirmed in store_settings. Test keys always work.

# =====================================================================================================
# 3) PLATFORM-INJECTED — do not set
# =====================================================================================================
# SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
# The service-role key bypasses Row Level Security. It must only ever exist inside Edge Functions.
